---
/**
 * /en/docs/ — English edition of the docs-area home page.
 * Intro: the philosophy of the differences — the compatibility is tested,
 * but the machinery is different. Four cards carry English titles + one-liners
 * and link to the Chinese articles for now ("in Chinese for now").
 */
import DocsLayout from '../../../components/DocsLayout.astro';

const articles = [
  {
    href: '/docs/compatibility/',
    title: 'Compatibility overview: what 83/83 means',
    line: 'A 100% pass across GNU Bash\'s 83 upstream test corpora, with 82 suites byte-identical in output — the one remaining delta proven byte-for-byte to be GNU\'s own coproc race.',
  },
  {
    href: '/docs/paths-and-msys/',
    title: 'Paths & MSYS: the biggest behavioral difference',
    line: 'One engine accepts all four path dialects — Windows, MSYS, WSL, Cygwin; with no MSYS runtime, argv arrives byte-for-byte as typed. MSYS_NO_PATHCONV is a word that does not exist here.',
  },
  {
    href: '/docs/execution-model/',
    title: 'Execution model: three tiers, zero forks',
    line: '( list ) and $( ) never create a process; the fd table replicates POSIX dup semantics; real processes appear only at real process boundaries — and everything a script can observe matches GNU Bash.',
  },
  {
    href: '/docs/performance-model/',
    title: 'Performance profile: where it is fast, where it is even',
    line: 'The zero-fork payoff lands on command substitution, subshells and background jobs; parity with GNU on external processes is the honest floor — every number measured on the same machine, methods public, benchmarks shipped along.',
  },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Docs · Where niubash differs from bash"
  description="The UNIXWIN docs area: niubash vs GNU Bash compatibility overview, path and MSYS behavioral differences, the zero-fork three-tier execution model, and the performance profile."
  path="/en/docs/"
  lang="en"
  enPath="/docs/"
>
  <header class="doc-head">
    <h1>Where niubash differs from bash</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      One-sentence positioning: <strong>the compatibility is tested, but the machinery is
      different.</strong> Against GNU Bash's own 83 upstream test suites, the niubash engine
      (rubash) scores 83/83 passing, with 82 suites byte-identical in output; and underneath
      that verified compatibility sits an entirely different machine — a zero-fork, three-tier
      execution model, path folding with no MSYS layer, byte-for-byte verbatim argv, all four
      path dialects accepted, 62 real builtins plus 12 inlined coreutils, and a deliberately
      maintained <code>uname = MSYS_NT</code> compatibility persona.
    </p>
    <p class="lead">
      This section takes the two sides of that coin apart: which side is "behaves like bash"
      (with suite and byte-level evidence), and which side is "built differently from bash"
      (with architecture and contract documents). Whether you are migrating scripts, evaluating
      performance, or chasing down a behavioral difference — start from the matching article.
    </p>
  </header>

  <nav class="cards" aria-label="Docs area article navigation">
    {
      articles.map((a) => (
        <a class="card" href={a.href}>
          <h2>{a.title}</h2>
          <p>{a.line}</p>
          <span class="go">Read the full article (in Chinese for now) →</span>
        </a>
      ))
    }
  </nav>

  <div class="all-docs">
    <h2>Full documentation</h2>
    <p>
      This section covers exactly one theme: how niubash differs from bash. Installation,
      plugins, agent onboarding, platform support and everything else live on the official
      documentation site:
      <a href="https://unixwin.github.io/niubash/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        unixwin.github.io/niubash ↗
      </a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .doc-head {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .lead {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .lead strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .lead code {
    background: var(--bg-code);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.08em 0.35em;
    font-size: 0.88em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.8rem 0 2.4rem;
  }

  .card {
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    padding: 1.15rem 1.3rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .card h2 {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .card:hover h2 {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .card .go {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .all-docs {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .all-docs h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .cards {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
